From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:13:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(fetch): apply the auth storage state to the browser
 context

WIGOLO_AUTH_STATE_PATH reached fetchWithBrowser as storageStatePath, but
no context was created with it, so use_auth fetches ran as a logged-out
visitor (#526).

- Pooled path: a fetch with a storage state gets its own context on the
  shared browser, created with storageState and closed in the finally.
  Seeding a pooled context instead would hand the session to every later
  fetch that reuses it.
- Stealth path: the dedicated context is created with the storage state.
- CDP / hosted scraping browser: a new context is created with it; an
  existing remote context cannot take one, so it is driven as before and
  a warning says the state was not applied.

Unit tests cover each path and that a later anonymous fetch gets a clean
context; an integration test fetches a local page with a real browser
and checks the state's cookie is sent, and not sent afterwards.

Fixes #526
